================================================================================
INCOMPLETE — THE VERBATIM LICENSE TEXT IS NOT YET IN THIS REPOSITORY
================================================================================

Read this before making the repository public.

**What is decided and stated above is real.**  ADR-009 was accepted on
2026-08-07 and this file is the project's license grant: Spatial IDE is
AGPL-3.0-or-later.  Nothing about that is provisional.

**What is missing is the copy of the license that must travel with the grant.**
AGPL-3.0 section 4 requires that every recipient of the Program be given a copy
of the License along with it.  The verbatim text of the GNU Affero General
Public License version 3 belongs at:

    LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt

and it is not there.  Until it is, this repository names its license without
supplying it, and ADR-009's pre-public checklist item 1 is not discharged.

**Why it is absent, stated as a fact rather than an excuse.**  The session that
placed this file was working under a binding no-downloads constraint (the
operator is on a metered connection).  The verbatim AGPL-3.0 text does not
exist anywhere on the machine — this was checked, not assumed; see
LICENSES/README.md for exactly what was searched and what was found.  It was
therefore recorded as deferred rather than fetched, and **it was deliberately
not reconstructed from memory**: a legal instrument transcribed approximately
is worse than one honestly marked absent, and the GPL-3.0 text that *is* on the
machine is a different license that cannot be patched into this one.

**What must happen, and it is one command:**

    curl -o LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt

Then delete this notice, from the line of `=` above to the end of the file.

The same applies to CC-BY-4.0, which `docs/` needs — see docs/LICENSE.
